{
  "source": "50 CFR Part 679, Table 3: Product Recovery Rates for Groundfish Species and Conversion Rates for Pacific Halibut [80 FR 11910, Mar. 5, 2015]",
  "read_from": "Code of Federal Regulations, Title 50, Volume 13, 10-1-24 edition, pages 974 to 976 (govinfo.gov, CFR-2024-title50-vol13-part679.pdf, PDF pages 447 to 449). The table is printed as three page images; it was read from them by eye on 2026-11-13.",
  "notes": [
    "A rate is product weight divided by round weight. To obtain round weight of groundfish, divide the product weight by the rate.",
    "Pacific halibut rates convert to net weight (gutted, head off), not round weight. Round weight is net weight divided by 0.75.",
    "Codes 88, 89 (infested or decomposed fish, 0.00) and 98, 99 (discards, 1.00; 0.75 for halibut) are accounting codes, not products, and are not transcribed.",
    "The six flatfish with their own species codes (122 to 134) appear only on the third printed page, where every species has the same meal rate."
